REFUNDS = """## Rescheduling policy
If you need to reschedule your trip:
- A rescheduling fee of 25% will be charged.
- Rescheduled trips must be booked within 3 months from the original trip date.
- Rescheduling requests made within 3 days of the trip start date will not be accommodated.
## Cancellation policy
Cancellations will incur the following charges based on the time of cancellation:
- 7 to 10 days before the trip start date: 30% of the total booking amount will be retained; the remaining 70% will be applied toward a future booking.
- 4 to 6 days before the trip start date: 50% of the total booking amount will be retained; the remaining 50% will be applied toward a future booking.
- Less than 3 days before the trip start date: 75% of the total booking amount will be retained; the remaining 25% will be applied toward a future booking.
- No show: 100% of the payment will be retained. No refunds or credits will be provided.
## Medical policy
In case of trip cancellation or interruption due to a medical emergency:
- Guests must provide valid medical documentation to apply for a rescheduling or partial refund.
- Rescheduling due to medical reasons will waive the rescheduling fee, but standard retention rates (as per the cancellation policy) will still apply.
## Group medical emergencies
If a group of guests is unable to attend the trip due to a medical emergency affecting one or more members (for example, a child):
- Valid medical documentation must be provided.
- The entire group can reschedule without paying a rescheduling fee.
- If the request is made within 3 days of the trip start date, 25% of the total booking amount will be retained to cover operational costs.
- The rescheduled trip must take place within 3 months of the original date, subject to availability.
## Refunds due to external factors
A full 100% refund will be processed in the event of cancellations caused by:
- Issues on our end, such as overbooking.
- Cancellation due to bad weather, communicated before the trip starts.
Refunds are processed to the original payment method. For any questions, call or WhatsApp us on +91 89287 94380."""

TERMS = """Version 2026-11-13. Last updated 13 November 2026.
These terms apply to every Rock & Anchor experience: treks, stargazing, village experiences, outdoor learning, school and corporate programmes, and custom experiences. Details that differ from one experience to another, such as timings, age limits, food, stay and what to bring, are on each experience page and in its FAQs. Please read both before you book.
## Booking and payment
- A booking is confirmed once our team confirms it to you and payment has been received as agreed.
- Prices, inclusions and age limits are listed on each experience page or shared when you enquire.
- Age related or student rates need valid ID proof at check in.
- Group bookings with mixed age groups are charged on each person's category rate.
- We offer tailored programmes for schools, colleges, universities and companies. Contact us for details.
## Booking for other people
- You can book places for other people on the same booking, such as your children or friends. The person who books and pays is responsible for the payment and for giving us correct details for everyone on the booking.
- Only enter another adult's details with their permission. Adults you book for may be asked to confirm their own place before the experience.
- To book for a child under 18, you must be their parent or legal guardian. You confirm this, and accept these terms and our Privacy Policy, when you add the child to your account and when you book for them.
- Before each experience, the parent or guardian must confirm the child's emergency contact and any medical information. A child whose details have not been confirmed cannot take part.
- If you travel on the same booking as your children, you cannot cancel your own place and leave them booked without you, unless the experience is one that children attend on their own.
## Cancellations, rescheduling and refunds
Rescheduling, cancellation, medical and refund terms are set out in our Cancellation and Refunds policy.
## Health and fitness
- Please tell us before the experience about any medical condition, allergy or medication that could affect your participation.
- Choose an experience that suits your fitness and comfort. If you are unsure, ask us before you book.
- Health protocols will be followed as per government recommendations at the time of the experience.
## Children
- Age limits and guardian requirements are given on each experience page.
- Children must be accompanied by a parent or guardian, unless the experience page says the experience is run for children on their own, such as a summer camp. For those experiences, a parent or guardian books the child's place and stays reachable on the emergency contact they give us.
- Children may also take part through a school or organisation that has their guardian's consent.
## Safety on the experience
- Outdoor activities carry natural risks, including uneven terrain, weather, water and wildlife.
- Please follow the instructions of your experience leader at all times.
- Your leader may change the route, timings or activities, or stop an activity, when weather or safety requires it.
## Guest behaviour
- We reserve the right to refuse entry, accommodation or participation to guests whose behaviour disrupts the comfort and safety of others.
- Many experiences take place in villages and in people's homes. Please respect your hosts, their homes and their way of life.
## Nature and waste
- Leave every place as you found it. Carry back what you bring, do not litter, and do not disturb plants or wildlife.
- Many of the places we visit have no waste collection. Please bring food and water in reusable containers.
## Getting there
- Unless transport is included in your booking, you are responsible for reaching the meeting point on time.
- Mobile network can be limited in the places we visit. Please let your family know your plans before you leave.
## Indemnity
- Rock & Anchor shall not be responsible for any delays or alterations in the programme, or expenses incurred directly or indirectly, due to natural hazards, accidents, breakdown of equipment or transport, weather, sickness, landslides, political closures or any untoward incidents.
- Rock & Anchor shall not be responsible for any loss, injury or damage to person or property in connection with any accommodation, transportation, activities or other services, resulting directly or indirectly from any act of God, fire, accident, breakdown of machinery, equipment or transport, civil disturbances, strikes, theft, wildlife, epidemics, regulations, or any other causes beyond our control.
- Rock & Anchor does not hold insurance covering accident, sickness, theft or other loss. Guests are advised to arrange their own insurance. All baggage and personal property are at the guest's risk at all times.
- By choosing to travel with Rock & Anchor, guests acknowledge that Rock & Anchor and its employees, subcontractors and suppliers do not accept liability for any damage or loss of property, or injury (fatal or otherwise), during the experience, its activities, accommodation or transport.
## Questions
For any questions about these terms, call or WhatsApp us on +91 89287 94380 or write to hello@rockandanchor.in.
By confirming a booking with us you agree to these terms."""

PRIVACY = """Version 2026-11-13. Last updated 13 November 2026.
## What we collect
When you enquire or book with us, we collect the personal information you give us so we can plan and run your experience safely. This includes your name, phone number, email address and date of birth. For anyone on a trip, it can also include an emergency contact and any medical information, allergies or medication you choose to tell us about.
We use date of birth to apply age limits and age-based prices, and to know who is under 18.
When you browse this website, our hosting provider may automatically receive technical information such as your IP address and browser type. We use this only to keep the site working and secure.
## Consent
When you share personal information to make a booking, you consent to us using it for that purpose only. If we ask for your information for another reason, such as marketing, we will ask you directly or give you a chance to say no.
You can withdraw your consent at any time by writing to hello@rockandanchor.in.
## Children and people you book for
When a parent or guardian adds a child under 18 to their account, they give us the child's name, date of birth, emergency contact and any medical information, and they consent on the child's behalf. Only that parent or guardian, our team and the leaders of the child's experiences can see these details. Children do not have their own account, and we do not send a child's medical details by email.
When you add a child, you choose how long we keep their medical information: until their trip is over, for one year after their last trip, or until you remove them. Their name, date of birth and emergency contact stay with your account until you remove them. To change your choice, write to hello@rockandanchor.in.
When you book for another adult, give us only the details we ask for, and only with their permission.
A parent or guardian can ask us to correct a child's details, or to remove a child from their account, by writing to hello@rockandanchor.in. A child who has an upcoming booking stays on the account until that booking is cancelled or has taken place.
## Disclosure
We may disclose your personal information if we are required by law to do so or if you violate our Terms and Conditions.
## Payments
Payments are arranged directly with our team. Where a payment gateway is used, it handles your payment details under its own security standards and privacy policy; we do not store card data.
## Third party services
Third party providers we use only collect, use and disclose your information to the extent needed to provide their services to us. Links on this site, such as WhatsApp or Instagram, take you to services governed by their own privacy policies.
## Security
We take reasonable precautions and follow industry best practices so that your personal information is not lost, misused, accessed, disclosed, altered or destroyed.
## Age of consent
By using this site you confirm that you are an adult. Children under 18 do not use this site themselves; a parent or guardian books for them, as described above.
## Changes to this policy
We may update this policy from time to time. Changes take effect when they are posted on this page.
## Questions
To access, correct or delete personal information we hold about you, or to raise a concern, write to hello@rockandanchor.in."""
